From ba523a967f02a749c299e9e966c98111b27278b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Natanael Copa <ncopa@alpinelinux.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:52:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] s390/kvm: revert backports depending on __kvm_faultin_pfn()

6.12.114 pulled in upstream commit 3762e905ec2e ("KVM: s390: use
__kvm_faultin_pfn()") as a Stable-dep-of 5f9df945d4e8 ("KVM: s390: Fix
FOLL_*/FAULT_FLAG_* confusion"). It depends on the KVM faultin rework
from v6.13 (__kvm_faultin_pfn(), KVM_PFN_ERR_NEEDS_IO,
kvm_release_faultin_page()), which is not in 6.12, so the build fails:

  arch/s390/kvm/kvm-s390.c:4776:15: error: implicit declaration of function '__kvm_faultin_pfn'
  arch/s390/kvm/kvm-s390.c:4786:20: error: 'KVM_PFN_ERR_NEEDS_IO' undeclared
  arch/s390/kvm/kvm-s390.c:4806:17: error: implicit declaration of function 'kvm_release_faultin_page'

Revert it together with the backports built on top of it:

  cd78dd7fb054 s390/uv: Don't return 0 from make_hva_secure() if the operation was not successful
  f5b6a9fa37d0 KVM: s390: Fix FOLL_*/FAULT_FLAG_* confusion
  45a6af541323 KVM: s390: pv: fix race when making a page secure
  4f2fe83204ec KVM: s390: move gmap_shadow_pgt_lookup() into kvm
  151690151a25 KVM: s390: use __kvm_faultin_pfn()

This restores the gmap_fault() based DAT fault handling, which only uses
FAULT_FLAG_* flags and is thus not affected by the FOLL_*/FAULT_FLAG_*
confusion.

Signed-off-by: Natanael Copa <ncopa@alpinelinux.org>
